        {
          "n": 1,
          "marks": 1,
          "type": "mcq",
          "question": "If $A = \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\end{bmatrix}$, then $|\\text{adj}\\,A|$ is equal to",
          "options": ["$5$", "$25$", "$-5$", "$10$"],
          "solution": {
            "answer": "(A) $5$",
            "concept": "For a square matrix of order $n$, $|\\text{adj}\\,A| = |A|^{n-1}$.",
            "steps": [
              { "do": "Find $|A|$.", "math": "|A| = 2(4) - 3(1) = 5" },
              { "do": "Use $|\\text{adj}\\,A| = |A|^{n-1}$ with $n = 2$.", "math": "|\\text{adj}\\,A| = 5^{1} = 5", "marks": 1 }
            ],
            "mistake": "Using $|A|^{n}$ instead of $|A|^{n-1}$ gives $25$, which is option (B)."
          }
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "marks": 1,
          "type": "assertion-reason",
          "source": "Board-pattern",
          "question": "**Assertion (A):** The function $f(x) = |x - 1|$ is continuous at $x = 1$. **Reason (R):** A function that is continuous at a point is always differentiable at that point.",
          "options": [
            "Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.",
            "Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A.",
            "A is true but R is false.",
            "A is false but R is true."
          ],
          "solution": {
            "answer": "(C) A is true but R is false.",
            "steps": [
              { "do": "Check A: $|x - 1|$ is continuous everywhere.", "why": "Modulus of a polynomial is continuous.", "math": "\\lim_{x \\to 1} |x - 1| = 0 = f(1)" },
              { "do": "Check R: $|x|$ is continuous at $0$ but not differentiable there.", "why": "Left derivative $-1$, right derivative $1$." },
              { "do": "A is true, R is false, so the answer is option (C).", "marks": 1 }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
